<Project>

  <!--
    An unrecognised component is an error, not a warning.

    RZ10012 is what the Razor compiler says when it meets <SomeComponent /> and cannot resolve it:
    "Found markup element with unexpected name". It then emits the element as LITERAL MARKUP, and a
    browser silently drops a tag it does not know. Nothing throws, nothing logs, the page renders —
    and the component is simply absent. The only symptom is a feature that is not there.

    It has shipped three times in this repository, every time for the same reason (a component in a
    folder the consuming page did not @using), and every time it was found by a person looking at a
    screen rather than by the build:
      · <NewInvestigationWindow> in PlaceView — the button that opened it did nothing at all.
      · <EvidenceVoteWidget> in PlaceView — the place page showed the vote tally with no way to
        vote, found 2026-09-22 in a build log, not by anybody using the page.
    A warning did not stop any of them, because a warning in a solution build is invisible: an
    incremental build that recompiles nothing reports "0 Warning(s)" and reads as proof.

    So it fails the build instead. The fix is always one @using on the consuming page.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);RZ10012</WarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
